version: "2.0"
name: gnomon-probes
description: >-
  The M1.0 probe harness: one directory per probe and run.mjs to run them;
  results/ holds their output.
context:
  - >-
    Split out of packages/gnomon/.purpose (2026-10-27); path: values stay
    relative to packages/gnomon, the package root.
components:
  gnomon-probes:
    description: >-
      M1.0 probe harness (spec §19.1, research 29 §2). `node
      packages/gnomon/probes/run.mjs <id> [--out-dir d] [--timeout ms]` imports
      probes/<id>/probe.mjs (zero deps, no build), runs its default export with
      {id, platform, arch, probeDir, signal}, and writes a probeResult:v1 record
      to probes/results/<id>.<platform>.json. Throws and timeouts become verdict
      `fail`. Exit codes 0 pass / 1 fail / 2 partial / 64 usage. Probe ids match
      ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$ (no path traversal). p-harness is the self-test and
      its results are gitignored; real results are committed from hardware runs
      only. A `fail` on a ruling means a re-plan memo before dependent builds.
      S0 (TD-2026-10-29-746, #kernel-sea): run-s0.mjs runs p15-sea-peertoken
      (probe SEA gnomon.kernel.probe → stdio child → LOCAL_PEERTOKEN →
      SecCodeCheckValidity; plain node must fail), p16-se-ephemeral
      (non-permanent SE key, no presence, never in the keychain; records
      whether its toid blob reloads in another process) and
      p17-se-afterfirstunlock (permanent SE key, AfterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly,
      group SW4BMQ8PNL.gnomon.probe; an unentitled signed binary is refused),
      built from _shared/kernel/KernelProbe.swift by _shared/kernel-probe.mjs.
      GNOMON_PROBE_ADHOC=1 forces ad-hoc signing.
      Unsigned macOS probes: p10m-sbx-deny-mac (S29-03/04 sandbox-exec session
      denies + escape matrix), p11-ws-framing (RFC 6455 over node:http with a
      forked server child, 27 Autobahn-style raw cases, 4 MiB throughput, RSS
      and phys_footprint), p-noise-vectors (Noise IK/XX/XXpsk3 over node:crypto
      against a verbatim cacophony/snow vector subset in vectors.json, G-LNK-11)
      p-log-fsync (kernel-log head-anchor fsync stalls, arms A-G; arm G =
      the research 33 policy: coalesced anchor + forced fullfsync+anchor at
      1/64, judged by the restated G-LOG-04; env P_LOG_FSYNC_ARMS accepts
      A,E,G) and p01-claude-cli (read-only `claude --version`/`--help` flag check;
      live items pending-manual). M1.0 batch 2 (probes/README.md lists them):
      unattended p06-local-caps (llama.cpp /slots n_ctx + live tool-call
      detection; no endpoint = partial, recorded not failed), p09-ed25519-matrix
      (WebCrypto Ed25519 in Node + every local engine under the §11.2 CSP;
      safari.html for Safari by hand, P09_SAFARI_LINE to record it),
      p12-excalidraw-csp (pinned Excalidraw bundled by esbuild in a temp dir,
      loaded under the §11.2 CSP; violations by phase, size, parse time),
      p14-link-outbound (default-deny sandbox-exec link profile), p03-pipe-dacl
      (win32, W1: Node cannot adopt a foreign pipe, the default pipe DACL lets Everyone and
      Anonymous read, a WRITE_DAC client handle makes it owner-only pipe-wide, a squatted
      name fails the listen EADDRINUSE); founder-run
      p00-sign-notary, p04-se-helper, p05-keychain-acl (signed
      GnomonHelperProbe.app from _shared/helper/ProbeHelper.swift; fail fast
      with a founder-steps pointer when the identity / provisioning profile /
      gnomon-notary profile is missing; prompt-free halves run unattended),
      p07-launch-token (NSWorkspace hand-off, eslogger + log stream + ps
      capture with an argv positive control, browser history grep incl.
      mozlz4), p01-claude-cli-manual (hook session_id, control_request
      interrupt, loopback-override observation, managed policy; claude by the
      path p01 recorded, never PATH). s29-10-voice-custody is a README stub
      pending the signed helper. p14b-link-fdpass (research paradigm-8/37):
      the kernel stand-in dials the peer and passes the connected socket over
      IPC to a deny-default child with no network* allow; full duplex 4 MiB,
      peer close, redial hand-off, child connect/UDP/listen/unix/file/exec all
      EPERM. p14b-web-handoff (T-2026-10-18-020): the inbound twin — the
      kernel stand-in listens on 127.0.0.1 (pauseOnConnect) and hands each
      accepted socket to a deny-default child with no network-* rule; full
      duplex 4 MiB, client close, 5 repeated hand-offs, every child
      bind/listen (0.0.0.0, ::, en0, 127.0.0.1, ::1, no host), UDP bind,
      outbound TCP and unix connect EPERM; pass on darwin. p-replay-order
      (T-2026-10-21-008, re-review M-1/M-4, darwin, real pinned claude, haiku):
      the ordering of SENT, replay, message_start/stop, tool_result and result
      for a queued message (during a tool call, after the final message_stop,
      back to back, inside a Stop-hook continuation) and for a blocking Stop
      hook with and without --include-hook-events; finding: the replay line is
      written on consumption, never on receipt, and hook_response lines appear
      only with --include-hook-events (exit_code 2, outcome 'error'). probes/_shared/ (browser.mjs, signing.mjs, abort.mjs — synchronous
      cleanups on SIGINT/SIGTERM/ctx.signal for founder-run probes, ask()
      rejects on abort — wkwebview-load.swift, helper/) is shared code, not a
      probe id. p12 pins its whole tree with a committed package-lock.json
      (npm ci). CI probe results go to $RUNNER_TEMP, never probes/results/.
    path: probes/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, probes, m1.0]
    tests:
      - test/probe-harness.test.ts
